-# Safarnama
\ No newline at end of file
+# Safarnama 🗺️ - Production-Ready Architecture
+
+Safarnama is a scalable, professional-grade discovery platform for India's offbeat travel spots.
+
+## 🏗️ Architecture (Clean Architecture)
+The project follows Clean Architecture principles to ensure scalability and maintainability:
+- **`src/api/`**: RESTful API endpoints (Flask Blueprints).
+- **`src/services/`**: Business logic layer.
+- **`src/repositories/`**: Data access layer (Repository Pattern).
+- **`src/models/`**: SQLAlchemy models with UUIDs and many-to-many relationships.
+- **`src/core/`**: Centralized configuration and settings.
+- **`src/schemas/`**: Pydantic schemas for request/response validation.
+
+## 🗄️ Database Schema (V2)
+The schema has been expanded to a granular geo-hierarchy:
+- **Location**: Country ➔ State ➔ District ➔ City ➔ Village.
+- **Classification**: Categories, Subcategories, Tags, and Activities.
+- **Place Details**: Latitude/Longitude (PostGIS ready), altitude, crowd factor, safety rating, and detailed descriptions.
+
+## 🚀 Getting Started
+
+### 1. Prerequisites
+- Python 3.11+
+- Virtual Environment
+
+### 2. Installation
+```bash
+python3 -m venv venv
+source venv/bin/activate
+pip install -r requirements.txt
+```
+
+### 3. Initialize & Seed Database
+```bash
+export PYTHONPATH=$PYTHONPATH:.
+python3 src/db/seed_v2.py
+```
+
+### 4. Run the Application
+```bash
+export PYTHONPATH=$PYTHONPATH:.
+python3 main.py
+```
+The API will be available at `http://localhost:5000/api/v1/`.
+The Interactive Map is served at `http://localhost:5000/`.
+
+## 🛠️ Tech Stack
+- **Backend**: Python, Flask, SQLAlchemy, Pydantic.
+- **Database**: SQLite (V2 Schema, transition-ready for PostgreSQL/PostGIS).
+- **Frontend**: Vanilla JS, Leaflet.js.
